# L §8.4 RUN-DOMAIN, E §11 (tally 2.1.7 R5, issue #144; #112): a cut computed from a value after `on` is
# refused at that value, `known <d> is after the model's on <on>`, as known or as if alike; the other asks
# stand. 2.1.6's refcore answered at the later cut (3).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input a: int
input later: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 3 "s"
  later = 2026-06-01 "s"

ask c0: a
ask c1: a as known 2026-06-01
ask c2: a with known 2026-06-01
ask c3: a as known later
ask c4: a as if {known later}
=== expect c0 c3 c4
c0: 3
  cut 2026-03-01
c3: refused: RUN-DOMAIN known 2026-06-01 is after the model's on 2026-03-01
c4: refused: RUN-DOMAIN known 2026-06-01 is after the model's on 2026-03-01
  cut 2026-03-01
